  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday) \nIssued at 1020 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nGet ready for this weekend. Colder air will continue to filter in on\nSaturday as high pressure builds in with northerly sfc winds ~10kts \nand gusts ~15kts with northwesterly winds aloft. Despite the partly sunny\nskies, daytime highs will only reach the upper 50s to lower 60s.\nSunday will only be a tad warmer with lighter northerly winds. The\nweather story is really about this weekend's overnight low as we will\nhover around freezing. So be sure to take time to bring in sensitive\nplants, provide proper shelter to outdoor pets and check in on others\nto ensure everyone is prepared for the cold. From here, models \ndisagree on how how an upper level low over northern Mexico into TX \nwill evolve early next week as it slides eastward through the\nnorthern Gulf states. Daytime highs look to rebound back into the \nmid/upper 60s through mid week and lows should stay above freezing.\nStuck with guidance and kept with a dry forecast for now.",
